<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kurt Eisner</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1867">1867</a>–<a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kurt Eisner was a German journalist and Independent Social Democrat who led the revolution in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a> on 7 November 1918, proclaiming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> a republic and ending Wittelsbach rule. He became the first premier of the Free State of Bavaria. His assassination by a right-wing nationalist in February 1919 set off the upheaval that led to the short-lived Bavarian Soviet Republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kurt-eisner.jpg" alt="Kurt Eisner" width="320" height="516" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Robert Sennecke · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KurtEisner1919.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
